65:["$","$L6f",null,{"type":"multiple","children":[["$","$L70",null,{"title":"Where do FAQs go?","id":"where-do-faqs-go","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["At the bottom of the page they belong to, under a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"## Common questions"}],"\nheading, in an ",["$","code",null,{"children":"<Accordions type=\"multiple\">"}]," block. No\nstandalone FAQ page exists, deliberately: a question is only useful next to the\nmaterial that raised it. Every ",["$","code",null,{"children":"<Accordion>"}]," needs an ",["$","code",null,{"children":"id"}],"."]}]}],["$","$L70",null,{"title":"My page renders in dev but the build fails.","id":"renders-in-dev-build-fails","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Three usual causes, in order of likelihood: an ",["$","code",null,{"children":"import"}]," statement in the\nMDX (components are global; remove it), a literal ",["$","code",null,{"children":"<"}]," or ",["$","code",null,{"children":">"}]," inside\nMermaid node text, or children passed to ",["$","code",null,{"children":"<SourceLink>"}],", which takes none."]}]}],["$","$L70",null,{"title":"Do I have to add an anchor to every heading?","id":"anchor-every-heading","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Yes, on every ",["$","code",null,{"children":"##"}]," and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"###"}],", and an ",["$","code",null,{"children":"id"}]," on every ",["$","code",null,{"children":"<Accordion>"}],". Run\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"lint:anchors --fix"}]," and it writes the ids Fumadocs was already\ngenerating, so nothing moves; it just stops the ids from tracking the\nwording."]}]}],["$","$L70",null,{"title":"I need to move or rename a page.","id":"moving-a-page","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Add the redirect in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"next.config.mjs"}]," in the same PR, update the section's\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"meta.json"}],", and grep the corpus for the old path. A moved page with no\nredirect breaks every external link and every agent that cached the URL,\nwhich is most of the reason the old URLs are still routable."]}]}],["$","$L70",null,{"title":"Can I add a new component?","id":"adding-a-component","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Yes, in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"web/apps/docs/components/"}],", registered in the global MDX\ncomponents map so pages do not import it. Prefer reusing what is there:\na component used on one page is a styling choice, and styling choices\nbelong in CSS."]}]}],["$","$L70",null,{"title":"Which pages need a `<NextStep>`?","id":"which-pages-need-nextstep","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"Every reading-path page: Getting started through How-to guides, Why\nForge and Operate, and the explanation and contribute chains. Reference pages are lookup surfaces and end where they\nend. A reading-path page with no handoff is a dead end, and dead ends are\nwhere readers leave."}]}]]}]
